  16 `family` is a property (`&"biped"`, `&"vehicle"`, `&"bot"`). Rigs face -Z; anatomical left is -X.
  17 
  18 ## How animation works
  19 - A clip is a **pose function** of time: `fn(t) -> {BoneName: Vector3(degrees), "_hips": Vector3(metres)}`, plus a
  20   duration and a loop flag. Bones have identity rest rotations, so a pose is plain per-bone euler degrees:
  21   `+x` swings a hanging limb forward (-Z) and tips an upright bone (spine, head) back, so a forward lean is negative x
  22   on Hips / Spine; `+y` turns left; `+z` rolls the top towards -X. A new clip is one function and one `add_clip` line.
  23 - `tick(frame)` evaluates the current pose, blends from the pose that was showing when `play` was called (quaternion
  24   slerp, smoothstep over the blend time) and writes bone poses. Everything is a function of the number of ticks and
  25   of `frame`: the same calls give the same pose on every run (the self-test compares two runs).
  26 - **Locomotion**: with no action clip playing, `set_locomotion` decides. `mode = walk`: one gait from standing to a
  27   sprint, read from the speed AND the direction of `velocity_local` (see "The walking gait" below); off the floor
  28   (`grounded = false`) the air pose, by `velocity_local.y`.
  29   `mode = skate`: a still hockey glide below 0.3 m/s blending to the full stride by 2.5 m/s; skate blades are shown
  30   and the body stands 5 cm higher.
  31 - **Action clips**: a one-shot clip returns to locomotion when it ends. `shoot` and `pass` are **upper-body** clips:
  32   while the rig moves faster than 0.8 m/s the legs keep the locomotion pose and only spine, arms and head take the
  33   action. `fall` and `skate_stop` **hold** their last pose until another `play` (`play(&"")` returns to locomotion).
  34 - A Skeleton3D that is posed outside the scene tree stops updating for good; the rig base works around it
  35   (`TLRigNode._flush` / `_reapply`), so a rig may be built, posed and ticked before it is added to the tree.
  36 
  37 ## Biped clips
  38 | Clip | Loop | Seconds | What it is |
  39 |---|---|---|---|
  40 | `idle` | yes | 4.0 | breathing, small head and arm drift |
  41 | `walk` | yes | 0.9 | lane-B walk, both arms swinging |
  42 | `run` | yes | 0.6 | forward lean, high knees, bent arms pumping |
  43 | `skate` | yes | 1.2 | hockey stride: deep knees, 36 degrees of forward lean, the pushing leg straightens out to the side and back |
  44 | `skate_stop` | holds | 0.4 | hockey stop: body snaps sideways, both skates across the travel line, lean away, head still facing travel |
  45 | `shoot` | no, upper | 0.85 | slap shot: wind-up to 0.30 s (stick back at shoulder height), contact at 0.42 s, high follow-through with the back leg lifting |
  46 | `pass` | no, upper | 0.55 | short low sweep, blade on the ice, contact at about 0.30 s |
  47 | `cheer` | yes | 1.2 | arms up in a V, two hops per cycle |
  48 | `fall` | holds | 1.0 | stumble, knees, flat on the front with the arms thrown forward |
  49 | `carry` | yes | 0.9 | both forearms held forward under a load (parent the load to `hand_r` or between the hands); with `set_locomotion` running the legs are the gait's (planted, at the real speed), without it the authored walk in place |
  50 | `work` | yes | 0.8 | hammering with the right arm, leaning in |
  51 | `jump` | no | 0.30 | take-off, played as the feet leave the floor: legs push straight, arms thrown up, ends in the rising air pose |
  52 | `land` | no | 0.45 | landing: the gait's own legs (feet stay where they stand, he may run on) under a crouch that takes the fall: soft from 4 m/s of fall, deep and slow with the arms out at 14 m/s. The fall speed is the last `velocity_local.y` seen while `grounded` was false. Its blend is at most 4 frames |
  53 | `slide` | holds | 0.30 | run slide: low on the left hip, right leg out ahead, left hand trailing on the floor, right arm up |
  54 | `slope_slide` | yes | 1.6 | sliding down steep ground: knees bent, weight back, turned a little across the fall line, arms out wide and working for balance. Loops until another `play` (`play(&"")` ends it) |
  55 | `air` | yes | 1.0 | the air pose by name (locomotion shows it by itself when `grounded` is false): rising above +4 m/s, apex round 0, falling below -5 m/s |
  56 
  57 With `stick = true` the arms of idle, walk, run, skate and skate_stop take the two-handed stick hold; `shoot` and
  58 `pass` always use it. The stick is a child of the `hand_r` socket; `socket(&"stick_blade")` is the blade (for a
  59 puck-contact test). The left hand is posed near the butt of the stick by hand-tuned angles: there is no IK.
