  67 ## Vehicle
  68 `set_param` every frame from the controller: `steer` (-1..1, + = left, 32 degrees at 1), `wheel_spin` (rad/s),
  69 `suspension` ([FL, FR, RL, RR] metres of compression: the wheel moves up relative to the body, clamped -0.12..0.16),
  70 `throttle`, `brake` (brake lights; both pitch the chassis a little), `nitro` (0..1: flame size, flicker keyed to
  71 the frame, light). Node tree: `Chassis` (Body mesh, Nitro, BrakeLights, sockets), `WheelFL|FR|RL|RR` / `Spin`.
  72 
  73 ## P3: what a rig looks like at game scale
  74 - The biped's head is 1.24 times larger and its hands 1.38 times (same 2.0 m of height; `TLRigBipedMesh.HEAD_K`, `HAND_K`). The face of pass 4 (eyes with
  75   highlights, brows, a smile, a blink every 204 frames) is unchanged; it is simply larger on the screen.
  76 - `prop`: what `hand_r` holds. `auto` = the hockey stick in `skate` mode, nothing in `walk` mode; `stick = true` is the same as `prop = stick`; `hammer` goes with `work`.
  77   A pack that built skaters with `mode = skate` and nothing else now gets a stick without any change. `headgear`: `auto` = in `skate` mode a helmet in the `top` colour
