  85 
  86 ## The walking gait (walker-feel, 18 Nov 2026; `biped/tl_rig_biped_gait.gd`, moves in `biped/tl_rig_biped_moves.gd`: internal to the rig, not pack API)
  87 - **The feet are planted by construction.** The gait is foot paths and the legs are solved (two bones, exact). A foot that
  88   stands has an anchor on the floor; each tick the anchor moves by exactly minus `velocity_local`, so the sole stands
  89   still at any speed, direction and acceleration. Feet land and lift at their exact phase part way through a tick (at
  90   9 m/s a tick is 15 cm of floor). When the rig is in the tree and its yaw changes, a standing foot keeps its place and
  91   heading in the world: turning on the spot, he steps round.
  92 - **Speed decides the gait** (m/s at scale 1; `velocity_local` is divided by `scale`):
  93 
  94   | speed | reads as | cadence (cycles/s, two steps each) | duty | stride on the floor |
  95   |---|---|---|---|---|
  96   | 1.0 | stroll | 1.00 | 0.64 | 0.64 m |
  97   | 1.4 | walk | 1.18 | 0.62 | 0.74 m |
  98   | 2.0 | brisk walk | 1.45 | 0.56 | 0.77 m |
  99   | 2.6 | jog (first flight phase: duty under 0.5) | 1.50 | 0.44 | 0.76 m |
 100   | 4.5 | easy run | 1.52 | 0.30 | 0.89 m |
 101   | 9.0 | sprint | 2.35 | 0.215 | 0.82 m |
 102 
 103   A walk at 4.5 m/s is not possible with 0.84 m legs (it would take 7.6 steps a second): 4.5 is a run with a flight phase.
 104 - **Direction**: the feet travel along the real direction. The pelvis turns 0.6 of the way towards it and the chest
 105   turns back, so he keeps facing forward: a sidestep is a side run under a forward-facing body. Past 100 degrees he
 106   backpedals (back to forward-style under 80 degrees).
 107 - **Standing**: the idle upper body over planted feet; stopping, he stands where the feet are and takes one or two
 108   settling steps.
 109 - **Pelvis height**: as high as the style asks (crouch and bounce by speed) and never higher than both legs reach, so a
 110   walk vaults over the standing leg and no leg is ever pulled off its foot.
 111 - Measure: `bash engine/tools/look.sh slip <speed> walk` prints `contact` (six sole points; a point on the floor two
 112   frames running should not have moved: mean / max m/s over the floor; frames with nothing on the floor; the lowest
 113   point) and the P3 `slip` line. 18 Nov: contact mean 0.03 to 0.10 m/s at 1 / 2 / 4.5 / 6 / 9 m/s, sidestep and
 114   backward at 4.5 (before: 0.94 to 9.2). The P3 meter samples the landing frame of a gait with a flight phase and reads
 115   high from 4.5 m/s up; trust `contact`. `RIG_ARGS="--dir=90"` sidestep, `--dir=180` backward, `--turn=60` a curve.
 116 - Clips of the moves: `bash engine/tools/look.sh clip rig:<jump|air|land|slide|slope_slide>:<speed>:0:<view> out.mp4`;
 117   views `behind` (the visitor's camera), `vclose`, `vfront` were added.
 118 - `stride_k` (cadence multiplier) still works; `amp_override` is kept for API v1 and has no effect (there is no swing
 119   amplitude to tune: the stride follows from the speed).
 120 
 121 ## A rig's shading travels with it (walker-feel)
 122 `TLRigs.build` sets the toon shader's instance parameter `tl_body` on every mesh of a rig (`engine/style/STYLE.md`, "Bodies
 123 that move"): mottle and hatching are anchored to the body, rim lights are drawn only on curved surfaces, a biped or a bot
 124 casts no shadow on itself (its shadow on the ground is unchanged), and the ink pass draws a body's contour at
 125 `ink.body_k` of the width. A mesh added to a rig after `build` (a prop parented to a socket by a pack) is a kit part and is
 126 shaded as the world is.
