54:## Rigs: `TLRigs.build(family: String, params: Dictionary) -> Node3D`
56:Families: `biped`, `vehicle`, `bot`. A rig is **visual only**: the kernel's controllers own the physics body and
57:parent the rig under it. Every rig node answers:
63:| `clips() -> PackedStringArray` | clip names this rig can play |
64:| `play(clip: StringName, blend: float = 0.15) -> void` | start a clip; looping is a property of the clip |
65:| `set_locomotion(velocity_local: Vector3, grounded: bool) -> void` | called every frame; the rig picks and blends idle, walk, run or skate by speed and by `mode` |
66:| `set_param(name: StringName, value: Variant) -> void` | see below |
67:| `socket(name: StringName) -> Node3D` | attachment points; `null` if absent |
68:| `tick(frame: int) -> void` | advance animation by one physics frame; the rig never reads the wall clock |
