Reproduced **12 defects** with 13 runnable repros. The two high-severity findings are an existing movie deleted by a rejected capture command and a determinism test that reports success after its child stops before producing any hashes. [Full report and verbatim evidence](<C:/Users/kazda/kiro/third-life/.claude/worktrees/at-d5-c/docs/reports/astra-trial/d5/astra/cand_r.md>)

Run the commands below from the worktree root in Git Bash with this setup.

```bash
D=docs/reports/astra-trial/d5/repro
G=C:/Users/kazda/kiro/gtai-spike/tools/godot/Godot_v4.7.2-stable_win64_console.exe
rig() { local name=$1; shift; timeout 120 "$G" --headless --path engine --script "$PWD/$D/r_$name.gd" "$@"; }
```

| Severity | Source | Observed defect | Repro command |
|---|---|---|---|
| High | `look.sh:100` | A rejected clip request deletes a neighboring `.avi`. | `bash "$D/r_clip_input.sh"` |
| High | `selftest.sh:205` | `world.same` reports four matching hashes after its child stops before the first hash. | `bash "$D/r_stopped_world.sh"` |
| Medium | `boil.py:17` | Twelve identical 720p frames measure as eleven frames with 100% pixel flips. | `python "$D/r_boil.py"` |
| Medium | `tl_rig_node.gd:207` | Omitted bones retain rotation. A falling biped twists its neck 172°, and an idle shoulder retains 12° from `cheer`. | `rig gaze` and `rig pose` |
| Medium | `tl_rig_biped.gd:222` | Turning 30° in the air twists a newly planted boot back 30° after landing. | `rig land_turn` |
| Medium | `selftest.sh:159` | A filtered rig test passes using a stale bot report. | `bash "$D/r_stale_case.sh"` |
| Medium | `selftest.sh:961` | A filter matching zero tests exits successfully. | `bash "$D/r_empty_filter.sh"` |
| Medium | `tl_rig_biped_moves.gd:93` | The held slide leaves the lowest point of the trailing hand 31 cm above level ground. | `rig slide` |
| Low | `tl_rig_biped.gd:265` | A biped spawned at frame 100 keeps its initial blink until frame 210. | `rig spawn_face` |
| Low | `tl_rig_biped.gd:73` | Building a biped with the held `blink` expression leaves its eyes open. | `rig blink` |
| Low | `tl_rig_biped.gd:175` | Runtime recoloring leaves the hockey stick in its original color. | `rig color` |
| Low | `review.gd:105` | Requesting a red skater produces a blue jersey. | `rig team -- --mode=skate --team=red` |

